UID:9bf603627d10b287578abd03529a31ae@guild.host
DESCRIPTION:Topic: Happy Town: Hanging out\, down the street. The same old
  thing we did last week.&#x20\;\n\nWhat do people do in third spaces? Ofte
 n\, they hang out. So how do we get people to hang out these days?\n\nIn l
 ess than a year\, happy town has hosted over 200 events run by our growing
  roster of 25+ hosts. We’ve had 6000 tickets grabbed\, and zero sales.\n
 \nMost events are recurring\, meaning many of these folks are hanging out\
 , again and again\, with many of the same people.\n\nYou might say we’ve
  turned events into “floating 3rd spaces” by making them more akin to 
 “hang outs”.\n\nIn this talk I’ll go over our guiding principles\, w
 hat we’ve learned so far\, and how I’m bringing this into our next pha
 se: creating the movement towards less lonely winter in Toronto.\n\n‎\n\
 nSpeaker: Adam Chen (in-person)\n\nAdam Chen works in mental health commun
 ications by day at HF Care\, and grow community by night with Happy Town. 
 He is a a storytelling and live journalism performer\, producer and direct
 or who dabbles in app development\, having co-created the private-blogging
  app “Smaller World." Website\n\n‎\n\nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome and
  Introductions\n\n7:20-7:50 Presentation and Q\\&A/discussion\n\n7:50-9:00
